
			PINOUT PROGRAM DOCUMENTATION

1)  IN ORDER TO USE THIS PROGRAM YOU MUST FIRST TRANSFER IT TO ONE OF THE   
    DISKS LABELED "PALASM2 PROGRAMS".  

2)  WHEN YOU EXICUTE THE PINOUT PROGRAM IT WILL GET THE INFORMATION ABOUT
    PIN NAMES AND THE PAL TYPE FROM THE FILE PALASM2.TRE.  THIS FILE IS 
    CREATED WHENEVER YOU RUN THE PALASM2 ASSEMBLER.  DUE TO THIS FACT YOU
    MUST RUN THE PALASM2 ASSEMBLER ON THE FILE BEFORE YOU RUN THE PINOUT
    PROGRAM.  

3)  ONCE THE PROGRAM HAS STARTED IT WILL ASK YOU IF YOU WANT THE FILE TO 
    BE SENT TO THE PRINTER AND THE DISK OR JUST TO THE DISK.  IF THE 
    PRINTER IS NOT CONNECTED OR YOU DO NOT WISH TO KEEP A HARD COPY OF 
    THE PINOUT RESPOND WITH A "D" FOR DISK ONLY.  THE FILE NAME WILL BE
    THE SAME AS THE ORIGINAL '.PDS' FILE WITH AN EXTENSION OF '.PIN'. 
    IF YOU DO WISH TO PRINT THE FILE AT THE TIME THAT YOU ARE RUNNING THE
    PROGRAM ENTER A "P" FOR PRINTER AND DISK.  YOU WILL THEN BE ASKED IF 
    YOU HAVE AN IBM OR EQUIVILENT PRINTER.  IF THE ANSWER TO THIS IS YES
    THE PROGRAM WILL SEND SPECIAL CHARACTERS TO THE PRINTER THAT WILL 
    MAKE A MUCH NICER LOOKING PICTURE.  IF YOU GET ITALICS OR OTHER 
    GARBAGE WHEN YOU ANSWER YES TO THE IBM PRINTER PROMPT YOU WERE WRONG
    OR THE PRINTER IS SETUP WRONG.  TRY THE PROGRAM AGAIN AND ANSWER NO
    TO THIS PROMPT.  WHAT YOU SHOULD GET AT THIS POINT WOULD BE A SERIES
    OF '*' CHARACTERS FORMING A DUAL INLINE PACKAGE DRAWING WITH THE PIN
    NAMES THAT YOU ASSIGNED.

4)  IF YOU CONTINUE TO HAVE TROUBLE OR IF YOU HAVE SUGESTIONS FOR UPDATES
    TO THIS PROGRAM CALL:

